# Everything on one machine. Copy this to `.env` and `docker compose up -d` is the whole command:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Compose reads `.env` on its own, so nothing here needs exporting and no command needs a flag.
# It carries two kinds of thing: which files make up the deployment, and the handful of values
# Compose substitutes into them. Secrets stay out of it — those live in env/vusan.env,
# env/workspace.env and env/sites.env, one per service, and each service sees only its own.
#
# For one service on a machine of its own, ignore this file entirely and follow docs/workspace.md
# or docs/sites.md; a machine of its own is still the recommendation for both.

# the four files, in order: the bot, the workspace, the site host, then the override that separates
# their networks. Drop a service you are not running from this list, together with its env file.
COMPOSE_FILE=compose.yaml:compose.workspace.yaml:compose.sites.yaml:compose.all.yaml

# --- the bot ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# where the database, the avatar and the personality files live, relative to this directory.
# Create it before the first start — `mkdir -p data` — a bind mount Docker creates is root-owned
# and the bot runs as uid 1000.
# VUSAN_HOST_DIR=./data

# --- the workspace -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# on one machine the bot reaches the controller by name over the compose network, so this published
# port is only for your own `curl` from the host. Keep it on loopback.
WORKSPACE_BIND=127.0.0.1

# --- the site host -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# required. a person's site lands on <their id>.<this domain>, the publishing API on api.<this
# domain>. Both must be proxied `A` records pointing at this machine. See docs/sites.md.
SITES_DOMAIN=

# deliberately not `./data`, which is VUSAN_HOST_DIR above: published pages are the least trusted
# content in the deployment and have no business beside the bot's database and credentials.
# Create it before the first start — `mkdir -p sites-data` — because a bind mount Docker creates
# comes out owned by root while the service runs as uid 1000.
SITES_HOST_DIR=./sites-data

# the certificate, its key and the origin-pull CA. See docs/sites.md for what goes in it.
SITES_CERT_DIR=./certs

# `off` where Cloudflare is not in front of this host: nothing else can present the client
# certificate Authenticated Origin Pulls asks for. See docs/sites.md#without-cloudflare.
# SITES_ORIGIN_PULLS=on

# --- images ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# every image comes from the registry by default. `docker compose up --build -d` builds all four
# from this checkout instead, and `docker compose pull` puts the published ones back.
# VUSAN_IMAGE=ghcr.io/helltar/vusan:latest
# WORKSPACE_IMAGE=ghcr.io/helltar/vusan-workspace:latest
# SITES_IMAGE=ghcr.io/helltar/vusan-sites:latest
# SITES_NGINX_IMAGE=ghcr.io/helltar/vusan-sites-nginx:latest
